// #2900: `String::to_lower` / `String::to_upper` are ordinary vibe functions in
// `lib/@vibe/builtin/string.vibe`, not builtins. The checker used to type them
// unconditionally, so this program passed `vibe check` and then died in codegen
// with `reached code generation unresolved` -- a message that blames the
// compiler for a program whose only fault is a missing import. They are refused
// here like their five siblings (`String::replace`, `replace_all`,
// `trim_start`, `trim_end`, `count`), and the message names the import.
fn main() -> Unit allows Console {
  println(String::to_lower("ABC"))
}
